                <pb facs="0132" n="98" xml:id="pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/3–1952</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea (Muccio) to the Deputy Assistant Secretary of
                        State for Far Eastern Affairs (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>official-informal</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pusan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-03-19">March 19, 1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Alex</hi>: I am enclosing for your personal background information a
                    memorandum prepared by Phil Manhard
                    commenting on the problem of the Chinese POWs
                    on Koje-do. A few days back, I arranged for him to give similar impressions to
                        General Yount in my presence in
                    even more detail than he has in the enclosed memorandum. General Yount also wants Phil to talk
                    directly to General Dodd, now in
                    overall command on the island.</p>
                <p>General Yount appreciates that there are
                    many unsatisfactory aspects to the situation on the island. He does not have
                    full confidence in the trustees and interpreters who are the go-betweens for the
                    Americans and the Chinese prisoners themselves. He is now studying measures that
                    might be more effective in making American policy and aims better known directly
                    to the prisoners so as to make it more difficult for the interpreters or
                    trustees to distort or shade the UN Command position.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >John</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d63-a1.xml" xpointer="d63-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
